:MachineLearning rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :AI4SEConcept ;
    rdfs:label "Machine Learning"@en ;
    skos:definition "Algorithms and statistical models enabling computer systems to learn from data and improve performance on tasks without explicit programming, applied to e-commerce problems"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Personalization increases revenue 10-30%"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Automates complex decision-making"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Scales to millions of users"@en ;
    :hasChallenge "Requires large training datasets"@en ;
    :hasChallenge "Model drift over time"@en ;
    :usesTool :TensorFlow ;
    :usesTool :PyTorch ;
    :usesTool :ScikitLearn ;
    :fashionRetailExample """Trendyol ML applications:
    1. Recommendation engine:
        - Collaborative filtering on 50M users
        - Product embeddings (512-dim vectors)
        - Real-time scoring (100ms p95)
        - Conversion uplift: +25%
    2. Demand forecasting:
        - LSTM model on 3 years historical data
        - Features: Seasonality, trends, promotions
        - Accuracy: MAPE <15%
        - Impact: Reduced overstock 30%
    3. Dynamic pricing:
        - Reinforcement learning
        - Maximize revenue while maintaining competitiveness
        - Price updates: Hourly
    4. Size recommendation:
        - Fit prediction based on customer measurements
        - Returns reduction: 22%
    5. Visual search:
        - CNN for image similarity
        - Upload photo → find similar products
    - ML Platform: MLflow for experiment tracking
    - Infrastructure: 50 GPU instances (AWS p3)
    - Team: 30 ML engineers + 15 data scientists"""@en ;
    :hasResource [
        :downloadURL <https://scikit-learn.org/stable/tutorial/index.html> ;
        rdfs:label "Scikit-Learn Tutorial"@en
    ] ;
    :hasResource [
        :downloadURL <https://www.tensorflow.org/guide> ;
        rdfs:label "TensorFlow Guide"@en
    ] .

:RecommendationSystems rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :MachineLearning ;
    rdfs:label "Recommendation Systems"@en ;
    skos:definition "ML systems suggesting relevant products to users based on behavior, preferences, and similarity to other users, critical for e-commerce personalization"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Increases AOV (average order value) 20-35%"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Improves discovery of long-tail products"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Increases session duration"@en ;
    :fashionRetailExample """LC Waikiki recommendation system:
    - Algorithms:
        - Collaborative filtering: User-user and item-item
        - Content-based: Product attributes similarity
        - Hybrid: Weighted combination
        - Deep learning: Two-tower neural network
    - Data:
        - 10M users
        - 200K products
        - 500M interactions (views, clicks, purchases)
    - Features:
        - Homepage: "Recommended for You" (6 items)
        - Product page: "Similar Items" (12 items)
        - Cart: "Complete the Look" (4 items)
        - Email: Personalized product grids
    - A/B testing:
        - Control: Random products
        - Treatment: ML recommendations
        - Conversion lift: +28%
        - Revenue lift: +35% (higher AOV)
    - Cold start problem: New users see trending items
    - Diversity: Ensure recommendations across categories
    - Real-time: 50ms p95 latency"""@en ;
    :hasResource [
        :downloadURL <https://developers.google.com/machine-learning/recommendation> ;
        rdfs:label "Google ML - Recommendation Systems"@en
    ] .

:NaturalLanguageProcessing rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :MachineLearning ;
    rdfs:label "Natural Language Processing (NLP)"@en ;
    skos:definition "ML techniques for understanding, interpreting, and generating human language, applied to product search, chatbots, and sentiment analysis in e-commerce"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Better search relevance (+40% conversion)"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Automated customer support (60% tickets)"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Understanding customer sentiment"@en ;
    :usesTool :spaCy ;
    :usesTool :HuggingFaceTransformers ;
    :usesTool :NLTK ;
    :fashionRetailExample """Hepsiburada NLP applications:
    1. Product search:
        - Turkish language model (BERT-based)
        - Query understanding:
            - "kırmızı elbise" → red dress
            - "büyük beden tişört" → plus size t-shirt
        - Typo correction: "elsbise" → "elbise"
        - Synonym expansion: "ayakkabı" includes "bot", "terlik"
        - Entity recognition: Brand, color, size, material
    2. Chatbot:
        - Intent classification: Order status, return, payment
        - Entity extraction: Order number, date
        - Response generation: GPT-based
        - Handles: 60% of customer inquiries automatically
        - Escalation: Human agent for complex issues
    3. Review analysis:
        - Sentiment: Positive, negative, neutral
        - Aspect-based: Quality, fit, shipping
        - Summary generation: 1000 reviews → 5 sentences
    4. Product categorization:
        - Auto-categorize from description
        - 90% accuracy across 5,000 categories
    - Languages: Turkish (primary), English
    - Infrastructure: Transformers on GPU instances"""@en ;
    :hasResource [
        :downloadURL <https://huggingface.co/docs/transformers/index> ;
        rdfs:label "Hugging Face Transformers Documentation"@en
    ] .

:ComputerVision rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :MachineLearning ;
    rdfs:label "Computer Vision"@en ;
    skos:definition "ML techniques enabling computers to derive meaningful information from visual inputs, applied to visual search, quality control, and AR try-on in fashion retail"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Visual search increases engagement 40%"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Automated quality control"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "AR try-on reduces returns 25%"@en ;
    :usesTool :OpenCV ;
    :usesTool :TensorFlowObjectDetection ;
    :usesTool :YOLOv8 ;
    :fashionRetailExample """Defacto computer vision systems:
    1. Visual search:
        - Upload photo → find similar products
        - CNN-based image embeddings
        - Cosine similarity search
        - 10M indexed product images
        - Results in <200ms
    2. AR virtual try-on:
        - Face detection and tracking
        - 3D pose estimation
        - Realistic rendering of glasses, hats
        - Mobile app feature (iOS/Android)
        - Usage: 5% of users, +40% conversion
    3. Quality control (warehouse):
        - Automated defect detection
        - Inspects 1,000 items/hour
        - Catches: Stains, tears, missing buttons
        - Accuracy: 95% (vs 85% human inspection)
    4. Auto-tagging:
        - Extract attributes from images
        - Color, pattern, style, occasion
        - Enriches product data automatically
    - Model: ResNet-50 fine-tuned on fashion data
    - Training data: 2M labeled fashion images
    - Infrastructure: AWS EC2 P3 instances"""@en ;
    :hasResource [
        :downloadURL <https://docs.opencv.org/4.x/> ;
        rdfs:label "OpenCV Documentation"@en
    ] .

:DemandForecasting rdf:type owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf :MachineLearning ;
    rdfs:label "Demand Forecasting"@en ;
    skos:definition "ML models predicting future product demand based on historical sales, seasonality, trends, and external factors, optimizing inventory and reducing waste"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Reduces inventory costs 20-30%"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Prevents stockouts (increases sales)"@en ;
    :hasBenefit "Reduces markdown/clearance needs"@en ;
    :fashionRetailExample """Koton demand forecasting system:
    - Model: Ensemble of ARIMA, Prophet, LSTM
    - Features:
        - Historical sales (3 years)
        - Seasonality (monthly, weekly, daily)
        - Promotions and campaigns
        - External: Weather, holidays, trends
    - Granularity: SKU-store-day level
    - Forecast horizon: 12 weeks ahead
    - Accuracy: MAPE <18% (industry: 30-40%)
    - Integration:
        - Inputs to inventory planning system
        - Triggers automatic reorders
    - Example: Winter coat demand
        - Historical: 5,000 units/month (Oct-Feb)
        - Forecast 2024: 6,200 units (warmer trend)
        - Actual: 6,100 units (98% accuracy)
    - Impact:
        - Reduced overstock 28%
        - Stockout rate: 12% → 4%
        - Markdown reduced ₺15M annually
    - Team: 5 data scientists
    - Re-train: Weekly with latest data"""@en ;
    :hasResource [
        :downloadURL <https://facebook.github.io/prophet/docs/quick_start.html> ;
        rdfs:label "Facebook Prophet - Time Series Forecasting"@en
    ] .

